      "title": "‘Did you send that report?’ The Icac bombshell that came late for Damien Tudehope",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/05/did-you-send-that-report-the-icac-bombshell-that-came-late-for-damien-tudehope",
      "description": "<p>The former Liberal finance minister was questioned by Icac counsel assisting, Peggy Dwyer, on Tuesday</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/05/australia-news-live-jetstar-charge-overhead-luggage-labor-tax-coalition-economy-wednesday-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The bombshell came in the last five minutes of former finance minister and rightwing powerbroker Damien Tudehope’s examination before the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/independent-commission-against-corruption\">Independent Commission Against Corruption</a> (Icac).</p><p>At 3.30pm on Tuesday, Tudehope was shown an email which he sent in February 2023, attaching a leaked draft parliamentary report into branch stacking in the Hills area by the Reformers, the shadowy group at the centre of Icac’s Operation Rosny.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/05/did-you-send-that-report-the-icac-bombshell-that-came-late-for-damien-tudehope\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-04T23:34:51"
    },
